WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:05.590
We are setting off on a journey fraught with dangerous notions--

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.269
eternity, the creation of all things from nothing, and

00:00:10.849 --> 00:00:15.279
dare I utter it, a word not to be thrown around with reckless abandon among those of reason,

00:00:16.429 --> 00:00:18.199
infinity.

00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:20.348
A case in point -- the library of

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:22.669
Babel.

00:00:22.669 --> 00:00:29.200
It is a library that holds every book that has ever been written and every book that ever will be written.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:35.140
Now here lies the madness: each book is filled with random strings of letters,

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:39.200
26 letters, commas, periods, spaces.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:45.340
And each book is different, but every volume in every one of these galleries has

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:53.140
410 pages.   Each page has 40 lines. Each line has 80 letters ex-alias,

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.620
that is to nothing but chance.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:03.000
So for every sensible line of straightforward statement, there are leagues and leagues

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.740
and leagues

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.460
of senseless

00:01:06.469 --> 00:01:08.300
jumbles, and incoherences.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.900
For example, one volume is made up in its entirety of the letters

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.340
M C V perversely repeated from the first line

00:01:17.899 --> 00:01:19.899
to the last.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:26.620
Another is mostly filled with gibberish until you reach the next to last page, when you see

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:30.220
Oh time thy

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.920
pyramids.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:42.100
It is unbearable knowledge that in some gallery on some shelf, a precious

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.580
cogent book exists yet remains inaccessible.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.140
And though one cannot know, my belief is the library stretches to - dare I say it -

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:53.869
the infinite.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:02:00.939
Many say I'm mistaken, that the possible number of books does have a limit, and while that number is beyond my understanding

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:09.850
I am gladdened by its distant  Hope  that however improbable, I may one day uncover

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:13.810
Meaning.

